  16: - One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.
  17: - The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.
  18: Rule
  19: - Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.
  20: - Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.
  21: - Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.
  22: Key insight
  23: - Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.
