  80: <description>
  81: Recolor every target pixel by following the ordered two-column substitution legend.
  82: 
  83: Input structure
  84: - A dominant background surrounds one multicolor vertical legend: a connected,
  85:   fully filled two-column block with one color pair per row.
  86: - Other non-background pixels or objects are the targets; divider or frame
  87:   pixels are ordinary target-side structure that remain unchanged unless their
  88:   color is rewritten by the legend.
  89: 
  90: Rule
  91: - Read the legend rows from top to bottom as substitutions from the left
  92:   column color to the right column color.
  93: - For each non-background pixel outside the legend, scan those rows in order;
  94:   whenever the current color equals the row's left color, replace it with the
  95:   row's right color and keep scanning lower rows.
  96: - Leave the legend itself and background pixels unchanged.
  97: 
  98: Key insight
  99: - The same color may be rewritten multiple times, but only by substitutions
 100:   that appear later in the vertical legend, so the row order is part of the
 101:   symbol instruction.
